ob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[19]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[19]},{"id":"azriel_561","name":"Azriel","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"ishmaiah_636","name":"Ishmaiah","also":"","summary":"Son of Obadiah, and viceroy of Zebulun under David and Solomon (1 Chr. 27:19).","verses":1,"father":"Obadiah","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"jerimoth_868","name":"Jerimoth","also":"","summary":"1 Chr. 27:19, ruler of Naphtali.","verses":1,"father":"Azriel","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"obadiah_2221","name":"Obadiah","also":"","summary":"A prince of Zebulun in the time of David (1 Chr. 27:19).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[20,21]},{"id":"azaziah_548","name":"Azaziah","also":"","summary":"The father of Hoshea, who was made ruler over the Ephraimites (1 Chr. 27:20).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"hoshea_1560","name":"Hoshea","also":"","summary":"1 Chr. 27:20.","verses":1,"father":"Azaziah","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"joel_1656","name":"Joel","also":"","summary":"1 Chr. 27:20.","verses":1,"father":"Pedaiah","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"pedaiah_2294","name":"Pedaiah","also":"","summary":".","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[21]},{"id":"abner_57","name":"Abner","also":"","summary":"Father of light; i.e., “enlightening”, the son of Ner and uncle of Saul. He was commander-in-chief of Saul’s army (1 Sam. 14:50; 17:55; 20:25).","verses":53,"father":"Ner","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"iddo_1593","name":"Iddo","also":"","summary":"Lovely.","verses":1,"father":"Zechariah","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"jaasiel_666","name":"Jaasiel","also":"","summary":"Made by God, one of David’s body-guard, the son of Abner (1 Chr. 27:21), called Jasiel in 1 Chr. 11:47.","verses":1,"father":"Abner","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"zechariah_3007","name":"Zechariah","also":"","summary":"A Merarite Levite (1 Chr. 27:21).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[22]},{"id":"azareel_371","name":"Azareel","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Jeroham","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"jeroham_879","name":"Jeroham","also":"","summary":"The father of Azareel, the “captain” of the tribe of Dan (1 Chr. 27:22).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"zeruiah_3055","name":"Zeruiah","also":"","summary":"Stricken of the Lord, David’s sister, and the mother of Abishai, Joab, and Asahel (1 Chr. 2:16), who were the three leading heroes of David’s army, and being his nephews, they were admitted to the closest companionship with him.","verses":25,"father":"Nahash","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"adiel_85","name":"Adiel","also":"","summary":"Father of Azmaveth.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"azmaveth_558","name":"Azmaveth","also":"","summary":"An overseer over the royal treasury in the time of David and Solomon (1 Chr. 27:25).","verses":1,"father":"Adiel","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"jehonathan_800","name":"Jehonathan","also":"","summary":"One of the stewards of David’s store-houses (1 Chr. 27:25).","verses":1,"father":"Uzziah","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"uzziah_2926","name":"Uzziah","also":"","summary":"The father of Jehonathan, one of David’s overseers (1 Chr. 27:25).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"chelub_930","name":"Chelub","also":"","summary":"Was the boss of farmers.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"ezri_1247","name":"Ezri","also":"","summary":"Help of Jehovah, the son of Chelub.","verses":1,"father":"Chelub","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"shimei_2690","name":"Shimei","also":"","summary":"A Ramathite who was “over the vineyards” of David (1 Chr. 27:27).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[27]},{"id":"zabdi_2956","name":"Zabdi","also":"","summary":"Called “the Shiphmite,” one of David’s officers, who had charge of his vineyards (1 Chr. 27:27).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[27]},{"id":"baal-hanan_577","name":"Baal-hanan","also":"","summary":"An overseer of “the olive trees and sycomore trees in the low plains” (the Shephelah) under David (1 Chr. 27:28).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"joash_1637","name":"Joash","also":"","summary":"One who had charge of the royal stores of oil under David and Solomon (1 Chr. 27:28).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"adlai_90","name":"Adlai","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"shaphat_2556","name":"Shaphat","also":"","summary":"One of David’s chief herdsmen (1 Chr. 27:29).","verses":1,"father":"Adlai","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"shitrai_2713","name":"Shitrai","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"jehdeiah_767","name":"Jehdeiah","also":"","summary":"A Meronothite, herdsman of the asses under David and Solomon (1 Chr. 27:30).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[30]},{"id":"obil_2234","name":"Obil","also":"","summary":"A keeper of camels, an Ishmaelite who was “over the camels” in the time of David (1 Chr. 27:30).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[30]},{"id":"jaziz_745","name":"Jaziz","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[31]},{"id":"jonadab_1688","name":"Jonadab","also":"Jonathan","summary":"Son of Shammah, and David’s nephew, and also one of his chief warriors (2 Sam. 21:21).","verses":7,"father":"Shammah","mother":"","v":[32]},{"id":"hachmoni_1337","name":"Hachmoni","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[32]},{"id":"jehiel_772","name":"Jehiel","also":"","summary":"A Hachmonite, a tutor in the family of David toward the close of his reign (1 Chr. 27:32).","verses":1,"father":"Hachmoni","mother":"","v":[32]},{"id":"ahithophel_162","name":"Ahithophel","also":"","summary":"Brother of insipidity or impiety, a man greatly renowned for his sagacity among the Jews. At the time of Absalom’s revolt he deserted David (Ps. 41:9; 55:12-14) and espoused the cause of Absalom (2 Sam. 15:12).","verses":17,"father":"","mother":"","v":[33,34]},{"id":"hushai_1577","name":"Hushai","also":"","summary":"Quick, “the Archite,” “the king’s friend” (1 Chr. 27:33). When David fled from Jerusalem, on account of the rebellion of Absalom, and had reached the summit of Olivet, he there met Hushai, whom he sent back to Jerusalem for the purpose of counteracting the influence of Ahithophel, who had joined the ranks of Absalom (2 Sam. 15:32, 37; 16:16-18).","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[33]},{"id":"abiathar_20","name":"Abiathar","also":"","summary":"Father of abundance, or my father excels, the son of Ahimelech the high priest. He was the tenth high priest, and the fourth in descent from Eli.","verses":29,"father":"Ahimelech","mother":"","v":[34]},{"id":"benaiah_443","name":"Benaiah","also":"","summary":"Father of Jehoiada.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[34]},{"id":"jehoiada_794","name":"Jehoiada","also":"","summary":"Succeeded Ahithophel.","verses":1,"father":"Benaiah","mother":"","v":[34]}],"places":[{"id":"anathoth_63","name":"Anathoth","kind":"City","lat":31.81291,"lon":35.2635,"summary":"The name of one of the cities of refuge, in the tribe of Benjamin (Josh. 21:18). The Jews, as a rule, did not change the names of the towns they found in Palestine; hence this town may be regarded as deriving its name from the goddess Anat.","verses":15,"v":[12]},{"id":"netophah_890","name":"Netophah","kind":"City","lat":31.73547,"lon":35.2205,"summary":"Distillation; dropping, a town in Judah, in the neighbourhood, probably, of Bethlehem (Neh. 7:26; 1 Chr. 2:54). Two of David’s guards were Netophathites (1 Chr. 27:13, 15).","verses":6,"v":[13]},{"id":"pirathon_949","name":"Pirathon","kind":"","lat":32.28602,"lon":35.02294,"summary":"Prince, or summit, a place “in the land of Ephraim” (Judg. 12:15), now Fer’on, some 10 miles south-west of Shechem.","verses":4,"v":[14]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[21]},{"id":"shephelah_1074","name":"Shephelah","kind":"Region","lat":31.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"region","verses":6,"v":[28]},{"id":"saron_1063","name":"Saron","kind":"Region","lat":32.63907,"lon":34.94593,"summary":"A plain, a level tract extending from the Mediterranean to the hill country to the west of Jerusalem, about 30 miles long and from 8 to 15 miles broad, celebrated for its beauty and fertility (1 Chr. 27:29; Isa. 33:9; 35:2; 65:10).","verses":6,"v":[29]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[4557,4557,4557,4557,3478,3478,3478,7218,1,1,8269,8269,505,505,3967,3967,3967,7860,7860,7860,8334,8334,4428,4428,3605,3605,1697,4256,4256,4256,935,935,935,935,2320,2320,3605,8141,8141,6242,6242,6242,6242,259,259,4256],[3434,1121,2068,2068,5921,5921,5921,5921,7223,7223,4256,7223,7223,7223,7223,7223,2320,6242,6242,6242,5921,5921,4256,4256],[1121,